  "question": "The power company needs to track the electricity consumption of each user. A user has an ID, name, address, and contact information. Each electricity usage record includes the record time, electricity consumption, user ID, and operator ID. An operator has an ID, name, department, and contact information.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0055\n\nCREATE TABLE `operator` (\n  `operator_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `department` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`operator_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `electricity_usage_record` (\n  `record_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `record_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `electricity_consumption` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `operator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`record_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `electricity_usage_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `electricity_usage_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`operator_id`) REFERENCES `operator` (`operator_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
